  "title": "Preserve reftable storage when constructing the isolated repository",
  "file": "scripts/push-git.sh",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A user delivers changes from a repository using Git's reftable reference storage. Delivery fails because the push wrapper cannot resolve the current branch, although an ordinary push succeeds.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "In a temporary fixture created with `git init --ref-format=reftable`, make an empty commit and initialize a local bare remote. Compare `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null push --no-follow-tags \"$url\" HEAD:refs/heads/baseline` with `bash \"$checkout/scripts/push-git.sh\" git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null push --no-follow-tags \"$url\" HEAD:refs/heads/wrapped`; also run the wrapper with the resolved commit SHA instead of HEAD.",
    "output": "Git 2.54.0. Ordinary push: exit 0, '* [new branch] HEAD -> baseline'. Wrapped HEAD push: exit 1, 'error: src refspec HEAD does not match any'. Wrapped explicit-SHA push: exit 0, new branch received successfully."
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD scripts/push-git.sh copies only `for name in objects refs packed-refs` and sets `core.repositoryformatversion 0`; it preserves object-format metadata but neither reftable storage nor `extensions.refStorage`. The production delivery path at src/pipeline/engine.ts:2117 explicitly passes \"HEAD\" to pushBranch. At base, worktreeGit executes the hardened Git command directly, without reconstructing repository administration, so Git retains its reference-storage configuration."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "If the factory's repositories use git's newer 'reftable' storage for branch names (for example because the owner set init.defaultRefFormat=reftable globally, or a future git makes it the default), any push that names HEAD instead of a raw commit id fails with 'src refspec HEAD does not match any'. Delivery then fails every time, even though the same push worked before this change.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "git init -q --ref-format=reftable src && cd src && git commit -q --allow-empty -m x && git init -q --bare ../dst.git && bash scripts/push-git.sh git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null push --no-follow-tags file://$TMPDIR/c1/dst.git HEAD:refs/heads/a; bash scripts/push-git.sh git push $url <sha>:refs/heads/b; git push -q $url HEAD:refs/heads/c",
    "output": "error: src refspec HEAD does not match any / rc=1 (wrapper, HEAD); explicit SHA via wrapper -> rc=0; plain git push HEAD -> rc=0"
   },
   "evidence": "push-git.sh:13-19 copies only `objects refs packed-refs` into the isolated common dir and writes only core.repositoryformatversion / extensions.objectformat; there is no reftable/ directory and no extensions.refStorage. So HEAD, which the worktree stores as a symbolic ref, can't be resolved. src/pipeline/engine.ts:2117 calls `pushBranch(..., \"HEAD\", ...)`, and pushBranch's sha argument defaults to \"HEAD\". The codebase already allows for reftable elsewhere (src/git/hardening.ts:276 checks extensions.refstorage)."
  }
 },
 {
